course: dictionary
lesson: 15799
title: Unattainable: too far away to reach
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can give you a clue. Un- often means "not", and to attain something is to reach or achieve it, so unattainable means something you cannot reach or achieve. «Her goal of climbing every mountain in one week was unattainable.» Nobody can do that, so the goal is impossible.
explain: Read the words around the word for more clues. «The prize seemed unattainable to the small team, so they did not even try.» The team gave up before they started because winning seemed impossible. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Impossible to reach fits, so that is a good meaning.
explain: Sometimes unattainable is used informally about a person. It means they seem too far above you to be friends with. «The popular boy seemed unattainable to everyone in her class.» The clues are how the children felt about him, not a goal they were trying to reach.
fact: Unattainable means impossible to reach, achieve or get.
fact: Informally, a person can be called unattainable if they seem too far above you to be friends with or go out with.
fact: «Unattainable standards» are levels of quality that almost nobody can meet.
fact: In maths, an unattainable score is one that cannot happen under the rules, such as 11 out of 10 when the top score is 10.
fact: Online, edited pictures can show unattainable bodies or lifestyles that most people could never really have.
exercise: «Her goal of running a marathon in one hour was unattainable.» What does unattainable mean? | Very short | *Impossible to reach or achieve | Easy to reach | Shiny and new
exercise: Your teacher says a score of 11 out of 10 is unattainable. Why? | It is the best score anyone can get | It is written in red ink | *It breaks the rules, because the top score is 10 | It is too low to count
exercise: Ella says unattainable means the same as easy. Is she right? | No, it means very old | *No, it means impossible to reach | Yes, it means nearly finished | Yes, it means easy to get
test: «Edited pictures online can show unattainable looks that nobody really has.» What does unattainable suggest here? | *Looks nobody can really reach or have | Looks that are very old | Looks that are easy to copy | Looks that are funny
test: «Seemingly unattainable goals can still be reached one step at a time.» What does seemingly mean? | It happens very quickly | It is certainly true | It is a loud sound | *It looks like it, but it may not really be so
exam: Which meaning of unattainable is correct? | *Impossible to reach, achieve or get | Short and rude | Very old | Shiny and new
